    "question": {
      ":question/id": "485105cc-ea89-524d-9beb-4565587032f6",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $C+D-E$, where\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,D=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 9 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,E=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 8 \\\\ -7 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n| $C+D-E=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Performing the operations on each corresponding entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C+D-E & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 9 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 8 \\\\ -7 & -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1+3-(-7) & 0+9-8 \\\\ -2+1-(-7) & 3+(-1)-(-7)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}11 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
